From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] setup: force libtoolize before autoreconf for riscv64

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 build infra, irrelevant to jeffdaily/parasail-python]

build_parasail() falls back to running a bare autoreconf -fi on the
downloaded GitHub archive snapshot of jeffdaily/parasail's master
branch, relying on autoreconf's own detection of configure.ac's
LT_INIT([win32-dll]) call to invoke libtoolize and seed m4/libtool.m4
(gitignored, not shipped in the snapshot) before aclocal/automake run.

On the riscv64 manylinux runner that auto-detection does not trigger
libtoolize: automake still auto-installs the ordinary missing
build-aux/ files (compile, config.guess, config.sub, install-sh,
missing, depcomp, test-driver) via --add-missing, but never installs
build-aux/ltmain.sh or m4/libtool.m4, so aclocal.m4 never gets the
libtool macros and automake dies on Makefile.am's lib_LTLIBRARIES with
"Libtool library used but 'LIBTOOL' is undefined".

Run libtoolize --force --copy explicitly before autoreconf so
m4/libtool.m4 and build-aux/ltmain.sh exist regardless of autoreconf's
own LT_INIT detection; this is the standard autogen.sh remedy for this
exact failure and is a no-op (same files, --force just re-copies them)
on toolchains where autoreconf's detection already works.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.py | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index 637214b..c3e4213 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -181,6 +181,16 @@ def run_autoreconf(root):
     if all_good:
         retcode = -1
         try:
+            # Force libtoolize to seed m4/libtool.m4 (and friends) before
+            # autoreconf runs: on some toolchains autoreconf's own
+            # auto-detection of LT_INIT fails to invoke libtoolize, so
+            # aclocal never picks up the libtool macros and automake dies
+            # with "Libtool library used but 'LIBTOOL' is undefined".
+            subprocess.Popen([
+                'libtoolize',
+                '--force',
+                '--copy',
+                ], cwd=root).wait()
             retcode = subprocess.Popen([
                 'autoreconf',
                 '-fi',
